{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/pulls/9514","id":4842068250,"node_id":"PR_kwDORmXBzs8AAAABIJwZGg","html_url":"https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/pull/9514","diff_url":"https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/pull/9514.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/pull/9514.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/issues/9514","number":9514,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"[physics-loop] analytic-fluid-construction bounded_theorem conditional-support","user":{"login":"JONbridgerapps","id":246726392,"node_id":"U_kgDODrS--A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246726392?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JONbridgerapps","html_url":"https://github.com/JONbridgerapps","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JONbridgerapps/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JONbridgerapps/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JONbridgerapps/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JONbridgerapps/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JONbridgerapps/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JONbridgerapps/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JONbridgerapps/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JONbridgerapps/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JONbridgerapps/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This construction asks whether an explicit scalar action can reproduce a supplied dust/radiation expansion history and have a controlled homogeneous future. It supplies a positive analytic three-field metric and potential, proves an exact tracking trajectory, and gives an energy/compactness argument for convergence to the unique vacuum for every finite-energy expanding homogeneous initial state with nonnegative fluids.\n\nThe actual current-surface status is **conditional-support**, claim type **bounded_theorem**. The action, universal matter coupling, fluid laws and vacuum scale are supplied. No observational likelihood is fitted or independently tested. This does not select the observed finite-time history, establish inhomogeneous or geodesic completeness, derive quantum theory, or establish a TOE. The later nonzero induced-curvature extension is outside this theorem.\n\n- [Complete proof and domain](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/75d8f001c8e055acd91383e3e088ead76f1851f2/docs/ANALYTIC_FLUID_COSMOLOGY_CONSTRUCTION_BOUNDED_THEOREM_NOTE_2026-10-13.md)\n- [Runner](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/75d8f001c8e055acd91383e3e088ead76f1851f2/scripts/analytic_fluid_cosmology_2026_10_13.py) and [input-bound output](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/75d8f001c8e055acd91383e3e088ead76f1851f2/logs/runner-cache/analytic_fluid_cosmology_2026_10_13.txt)\n- [Handoff](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/75d8f001c8e055acd91383e3e088ead76f1851f2/.claude/science/physics-loops/analytic-fluid-construction-20261013/HANDOFF.md), [trace](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/75d8f001c8e055acd91383e3e088ead76f1851f2/.claude/science/physics-loops/analytic-fluid-construction-20261013/TRACE_GATE.md), [claim certificate](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/75d8f001c8e055acd91383e3e088ead76f1851f2/.claude/science/physics-loops/analytic-fluid-construction-20261013/CLAIM_STATUS_CERTIFICATE.md) and [independent source review](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/75d8f001c8e055acd91383e3e088ead76f1851f2/.claude/science/physics-loops/analytic-fluid-construction-20261013/independent_source_review/REPORT_v1.md)\n\nThe trace is frontier_discovery with unknown_frontier reachability. No existing retained import or open lane is claimed closed. The older combined cosmology negative/history-selection packet remains deferred and recoverable, with its five-family delivery obligation unchanged. The focused prior-art search found no matching complete construction in the inspected sources; that is not a priority or novelty proof.\n\nVerification:\n\n- Canonical runner: **1497/0**, with unchanged declared note, fixture and import identities. Original mathematical/numerical reviews, real mutation trials and complete exploratory source recovery are preserved in the branch loop pack.\n- Full independent source review found no material issue within the bounded claim. Subsequent confirmations checked unchanged scientific bytes, the full original-to-final disposition map and final manifest. Parent read the reports and verified their bound artifacts.\n- Final review_receipt.py --cache passed for the **32-path tree 9ae2ad5a41716c42cf5a4f10ec8ff23e7935ef33**. The pushed commit has that same tree.\n- One isolated combined pass succeeded: bash docs/audit/scripts/run_pipeline.sh --stage-citation-manifest; python3 docs/audit/scripts/audit_lint.py --strict; python3 docs/audit/scripts/check_changed_audit_evidence.py --base origin/main --include-worktree. Changed evidence reports checked=1 failures=0 control_failures=0. Existing warnings/notices are preserved. Only one standalone zero-edge topology node is added.\n- Actual final reports, unit/gate commands, stdout/stderr hashes, source/input bindings and push record are under analytic_milestone_runtime/ in the [campaign recovery archive](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/4f349b09c2aff65dc9e55c9e040175c091b32b61/.claude/science/physics-loops/observations-to-toe-24h-20261012/milestones/direct_curvature_inverse_checkpoint_20261013/RECOVERY_v1.tar.gz), with its [per-member manifest](https://github.com/jonathonreilly/qubit-lattice-axiom-framework/blob/4f349b09c2aff65dc9e55c9e040175c091b32b61/.claude/science/physics-loops/observations-to-toe-24h-20261012/milestones/direct_curvature_inverse_checkpoint_20261013/RECOVERY_v1.json).\n\nProcess limitation: actual API discovery preceded canonical execution, but the full unit helper did not. That timing deviation is recorded in immutable reviews; later successful helper runs do not erase it. These source-review and mechanical results describe the actual preserved sequence.\n\nIndependent audit remains required before effective retained status. This PR is for review; no science has been merged or pushed to main.\n\n","created_at":"2026-10-13T10:47:57Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T10:47:58Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"9c61b3a09790b8176db8b655972a66ae2988a5ac","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"jonathonreilly","id":235930534,"node_id":"U_kgDODhADpg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/235930534?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathonreilly","html_url":"https://github.com/jonathonreilly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathonreilly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathonreilly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathonreilly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathonreilly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathonreilly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathonreilly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathonreilly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathonreilly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jonathonreilly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jonathonreilly/qub